      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission washing attachment with equipment</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;html xmlns:v=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml&quot; xmlns:o=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; xmlns:w=&quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word&quot; xmlns:m=&quot;http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2004/12/omml&quot; xmlns=&quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40&quot;&gt;     &lt;body lang=IT style=&apos;tab-interval:35.4pt&apos;&gt;  &lt;div class=WordSection1&gt;  &lt;p class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;span style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;span style=&apos;mso-spacerun:yes&apos;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;To perform automatic transmission washing, it is advisable to connect the equipment to the attachments shown in &lt;B&gt;Fig. 1&lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;1 &lt;/B&gt;- Attachment for parts-washing equipment&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;2 &lt;/B&gt;- Hole for checking automatic transmission oil level&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt;3 &lt;/B&gt;- Hole for draining the automatic transmission oil.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;  &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;/body&gt;  &lt;/html&gt;</Corpo>
