      </XFILE>
    </XCAPITOLO>
    <XCAPITOLO>
      <RifIDDoc>199217638</RifIDDoc>
      <Ordine>20</Ordine>
      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission oil filling procedure</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Position the vehicle on a level surface and lock the wheels &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Switch off the lighting and air conditioning systems &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Place the gear lever in &lt;B&gt; P &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Apply the parking brake &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Connect the diagnostic tester &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Remove the filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt; CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt; Always replace the filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; and its gasket &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Using the diagnostic tester, perform the procedure &lt;B&gt; &quot;Gearbox control system: oil compensation&quot; &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Refill with gearbox oil through the filler hole &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; following the instructions provided by the diagnostic tester &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Insert a new filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; with the relevant gasket, tightening to &lt;B&gt; 35 N·m &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Continue with the automatic gearbox oil level check procedure &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; </Corpo>
      <RifIDFileIMGANI>299007667</RifIDFileIMGANI>
      <Allineamento>R</Allineamento>
      <XFILE>
        <ID>299007667</ID>
        <Type>IMG</Type>
        <URL>GETFILE:299007667</URL>
      </XFILE>
    </XCAPITOLO>
    <XCAPITOLO>
      <RifIDDoc>199217638</RifIDDoc>
      <Ordine>21</Ordine>
      <Capitolo>Automatic transmission oil level check procedure</Capitolo>
      <Corpo> &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Bring the gearbox oil temperature to &lt;B&gt; 30° - 40° C &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Position the vehicle on a level surface and lock the wheels &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Switch off the lighting and air conditioning systems &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;LI&gt; Set the gear lever to &lt;B&gt; P &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Apply the parking brake &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Connect the diagnostic tester &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Remove the filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt;  &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt; CAUTION: &lt;/B&gt; Always replace the filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; and its seal &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Using the diagnostic tester, perform the &lt;B&gt; &quot;Gearbox control system: oil compensation&quot; &lt;/B&gt; procedure  &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Bring the gearbox oil to a temperature of &lt;B&gt; 40° - 50°C &lt;/B&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Follow the instructions on the diagnostic tester to perform the automatic gearbox oil level check procedure &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;B&gt; CAUTION:  &lt;/B&gt; An oil level that is too high or too low will compromise the operation of the gearbox. &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;LI&gt; Insert a new filler cap &lt;B&gt; B &lt;/B&gt; with the relevant gasket, tightening to &lt;B&gt; 35 N·m &lt;/B&gt;. &lt;BR/&gt; &lt;BR/&gt; </Corpo>
